    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλην</span></b> , acc. fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος</span>, used (se. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδόν</span>) as Adv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>elsewhither</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. καὶ ἄ. διώκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.1.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				26.3
			</span></i> : also of Time, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. καὶ ἄ.
				ἀποβλέπειν εἴς τινα</span>
			<i>again and again</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				273b
			</span></i>.</div>
